From: Coia Prant <coiaprant@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: xpcs: add ANRESTART support for SGMII link recovery

On some hardware using the DesignWare XPCS IP (e.g., RK3568 MAC side
SGMII), the PCS does not automatically restart auto-negotiation when the
link goes down and comes back up. Without an explicit ANRESTART, the link
stays down forever.

Add BMCR_ANRESTART in two places:
1. In xpcs_config_aneg_c37_sgmii(), when starting AN, clear the CL37 AN
   complete status interrupt and trigger ANRESTART to initiate a fresh
   negotiation.
2. In xpcs_get_state_c37_sgmii(), when the link is down and AN completion
   is detected, clear the interrupt and trigger ANRESTART to restart the
   negotiation process.

This is a backport of upstream RK3568 XPCS series patch 06 to the 6.12
tree. The 6.12 adaptation notes:
- 6.12 enables C37 AN through DW_VR_MII_MMD_CTRL/AN_CL37_EN rather than
  the MII_BMCR ANENABLE write used by the original v2 patch, so the
  ANRESTART is issued as a separate VEND2 MII_BMCR access.
- 6.12 has no xpcs_modify(); it provides xpcs_modify_changed(), which is
  used here to read-modify-write only the BMCR_ANRESTART bit so the
  remaining BMCR bits are preserved.
- MII_BMCR and BMCR_ANRESTART come from <linux/mii.h> (reached via
  <linux/phy.h>, already included by this file; BMCR_ANRESTART is already
  used in xpcs_an_restart()).

Signed-off-by: Coia Prant <coiaprant@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/pcs-xpcs.c | 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-xpcs.c b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-xpcs.c
index 0337e2bcc0125..28e98449e8ac2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-xpcs.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-xpcs.c
@@ -731,10 +731,33 @@ static int xpcs_config_aneg_c37_sgmii(struct dw_xpcs *xpcs,
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Clear CL37 AN complete status */
+	ret = xpcs_write(xpcs, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, DW_VR_MII_AN_INTR_STS, 0);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
 	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED)
 		ret = xpcs_write(xpcs, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, DW_VR_MII_MMD_CTRL,
 				 mdio_ctrl | AN_CL37_EN);
 
+	/*
+	 * The DW XPCS IP (e.g. on the RK3568 MAC-side SGMII) does not
+	 * automatically restart auto-negotiation when the link drops and
+	 * comes back, leaving the link down forever. Issue an explicit
+	 * ANRESTART (standard C22 MII_BMCR bit, accessed via the VEND2 MMD)
+	 * to initiate a fresh negotiation. The original v2 patch folded this
+	 * into the same MII_BMCR write that also set ANENABLE, but 6.12
+	 * enables C37 AN through DW_VR_MII_MMD_CTRL/AN_CL37_EN, so the
+	 * restart is issued here as a separate read-modify-write that only
+	 * sets the BMCR_ANRESTART bit and preserves the surrounding bits.
+	 */
+	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED) {
+		ret = xpcs_modify_changed(xpcs, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, MII_BMCR,
+					  BMCR_ANRESTART, BMCR_ANRESTART);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -1010,9 +1033,14 @@ static int xpcs_get_state_c37_sgmii(struct dw_xpcs *xpcs,
 	}
 
 	/* Clear AN complete status or interrupt */
-	if (state->an_complete)
+	if (state->an_complete) {
 		xpcs_write(xpcs, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, DW_VR_MII_AN_INTR_STS, 0);
 
+		/* Initiate the next round of AN */
+		xpcs_modify_changed(xpcs, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, MII_BMCR,
+				    BMCR_ANRESTART, BMCR_ANRESTART);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
--- 
2.43.0
